<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Václav Klaus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1941</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Václav Klaus is a Czech economist and politician who, as finance minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> from 1989, led its rapid move to a market economy, including voucher privatisation. He founded the Civic Democratic Party, won the 1992 Czech elections and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-meciar">Vladimír Mečiar</a> negotiated the dissolution of Czechoslovakia. He was Czech prime minister from 1992 to 1997 and president from 2003 to 2013.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vaclav-klaus.jpg" alt="Václav Klaus" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jindřich Nosek (NoJin) · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%A1clav_Klaus_(2022).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
